  "notes": "Behavior-compliance change on existing surfaces — no new members are introduced, so the inventory is the migration itself, the two Response-side delivery surfaces whose rejection/error values change, and the serialize/deserialize algorithm that governs which values survive. All spec algorithm text is quoted verbatim from the Living Standards fetched 2026-10-04. Known limits, preserved honestly on-page rather than invented: BCD has no entry for this change (api/Response.json checked, zero abort matches); the first compliant Firefox version and any Edge version are not recorded in the sources read and are stated as unknown in the compat table; per-browser WPT subtest results were not individually verified; the request-body cancellation side of §5.6 is noted but not claimed as part of the Chrome 154 delta since the ChromeStatus record scopes the change to the Response side."
}
